// Was SOUNDNESS QUEUE row static_mut_elided_struct_region_write_admits; closed: a write into a static's storage demands 'static data (E0597).
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row static_mut_elided_struct_region_write_admits (tier 2).
// NEIGHBOUR of bc_admits issue-69114-static-mut-ty, ROWED — reason 1 (the fact has
// no carrier there). `static mut HS: H` with `struct H<'a>` elides the struct's
// lifetime argument, and the elided argument has NO SLOT in the declared type: a
// fill of Struct lifetime args at the write closed nothing (measured 2026-09-13d),
// while the same program with `H<'static>` written is refused. Both writes below,
// the whole value and the field, are E0597 in Rust.
package static_mut_elided_struct_region_write_fail;
static V: i64 = 5i64;
struct H<'a> { r: &'a i64 }
static mut HS: H = H { r: &V };
fn set() {
    let n: i64 = 1i64;
    unsafe {
        HS = H { r: &n };
        HS.r = &n;
    }
}
fn main() -> i32 { set(); unsafe { return *HS.r as i32; } }
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 (round 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit, class CONFIRMED): REFUSED — error[E0597]: `n` does not live long enough. Twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/static_mut_elided_struct_region_write_admits.rs. Variants: static_mut_elided_struct_region_write_admits__static_written.rs REFUSED E0597. Audit note: elided H in static accepted by rustc; H<'static> spelling also E0597.
